#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:40
msgid ""
"An investments row supplies the selection identifying the table body, the"
" one identifying the fund name, the one identifying the currency, and the"
" column positions of market value, quantity, percentage of net assets and"
" acquisition cost:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:49
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The `set` columns are {doc}`../selections` in their compact textual form."
" The numeric columns are column indices, and negative values count from "
"the right — `-1` being the last column, which is what you want on a table"
" whose leading columns vary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:53
msgid "`additional_args.csv`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:55
msgid ""
"A second table, joined onto the first by `ID`, holding the parameters a "
"pipe usually leaves alone. **At most one row per pipe**, and no row at "
"all is the normal case — every column defaults, and a pipe that says "
"nothing behaves the way the library does."
msgstr ""

