#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:74
msgid ""
"The two tolerances say how far apart two cells may sit and still count as"
" the same column, or the same row. They are **independent**: leaving one "
"empty means zero for that axis, never the other one's value. A table "
"whose column of names breaks up because the names differ in length wants "
"a wide column tolerance and a row tolerance of zero — one number for both"
" would weld consecutive holdings into a single row while it was busy "
"reuniting the names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:80
msgid ""
"A column the table does not take is refused when the repository loads, "
"rather than ignored — a file written for an older engine would otherwise "
"carry cells that silently do nothing. So is a column that only refines "
"another one, filled without it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:84
msgid ""
"Each column belongs to one segment, and that matters: a pipe that "
"switches a segment **off** in `partial_pipes.csv` and then fills in one "
"of that segment's columns is rejected when the repository loads. "
"Declaring a segment off and configuring it is a contradiction, not "
"something to guess at."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:90
msgid ""
"How the table-coordinates algorithm finds the grid, when its default "
"choices do not suit a layout: `RETURN_ROWS`, `BIG_CELL_RULE`, "
"`USE_RULER_AREA`, `USE_TEST_POS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:93
msgid "The three `Collapse` cells"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:95
msgid ""
"A name too long for its column wraps, and the remainder arrives as a line"
" of its own with its own coordinates. Naming the column that may break "
"**is** asking for the collapse — with the cell filled the `pdf_extract` "
"emits one block per **cell** instead of one per line — and the other two "
"cells say how:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:100
msgid ""
"**`Collapse direction`** — `down` (the default) puts the pieces on the "
"**first** row of the run, `up` on the last. Pick the one that leaves the "
"cell beside **its own values**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:102
msgid ""
"**`Collapse algorithm`** — `pattern` (the default) takes every run of "
"consecutive cells of the column; `geometry` only the runs whose rows "
"carry nothing but the name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:105
msgid ""
"Several columns, because a page often carries **two tables side by side**"
" and then the column of names is two columns. The pieces are joined with "
"nothing between them, which is not a choice: the page already says how "
"they meet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:109
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{doc}`../adding-a-datum/parameters` shows the case on the page that "
"produced it, together with the trap — a heading in the column of names is"
" geometrically indistinguishable from a wrapped name, and a format whose "
"headings share the body's face wants no collapse at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:115
msgid ""
"`Geometrical indexing` decides what the numeric columns of `args.csv` "
"mean. `TRUE`, the default, makes them **linear distances on the grid**, "
"wrapping into the next row when they exceed the table's width. `FALSE` "
"makes them positions in the flat list of blocks — which shifts every "
"field of any row whose company name wrapped onto two lines, so it is "
"rarely what you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:122
msgid ""
"Several reports print `-` where a number belongs — a frozen holding, a "
"position too small to round to a visible percentage. That dash is not a "
"number, so by default the row is dropped (for the market value) or the "
"field left empty (for the others), and the `.log.csv` says so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:126
msgid ""
"Where you have checked the report and the dash really does mean zero, "
"this column says so, **one field at a time**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "Flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`MARKET_VALUE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "the market value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`QUANTITY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "the nominal quantity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`PERC_NET_ASSETS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "the percentage of net assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`ACQUISITION_COST`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "the acquisition cost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`ALL`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "the four together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:144
msgid ""
"The expression is the same little language `Algorithm flags` uses — `|`, "
"`&`, `^`, `~` and parentheses — so `ALL & ~QUANTITY` is the three fields "
"other than the quantity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:147
msgid ""
"**Per field, and not one switch,** because the need really is per field: "
"a report that prints `-` for a percentage it cannot show may print "
"nothing of the sort in the quantity column, and a single switch would "
"invent a quantity of zero there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:151
msgid ""
"**Only a dash.** The substitution recognises the dash family and nothing "
"else — `-`, `–`, `—` and their kin, alone or repeated, with any "
"surrounding space. Not an empty cell, which in these tables means "
"*absent*; not `n/a`; not a lone `.` or `,`. That line is drawn "
"deliberately: by far the most common cause of \"this cell is not a "
"number\" is a **misaligned offset**, where the engine is reading a "
"currency code, a header or a company name one column away from where it "
"should be. Those must keep failing loudly, and a rule that turned any "
"unreadable cell into zero would bury them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:158
msgid ""
"There is no flag for the acquisition **currency**: a dash there says \"no"
" currency\", and zero is not a currency. `ALL` does not touch it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:161
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The zero that results is a real value and behaves like one. It is on the "
"lower edge of its domain, which the engine notes at `debug` and not in "
"the `.log.csv` ({doc}`../../user/logging`) — zero is ordinary, and a file"
" that said so on every written-off holding would say nothing else. That "
"is the point: the holding is in the output, where it was being dropped "
"before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:168
msgid ""
"One regular expression whose matches are cut out of the sub-fund's name "
"before it becomes the sub-fund's identity. One cell and not a list: "
"several cuts are one alternation, `\\(continued\\)|\\(cont\\.\\)`, and "
"the space a cut leaves behind goes with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:172
msgid ""
"The commonest use is the **footnote mark**. Some reports hang a footnote "
"on a sub-fund's name in the heading of its own pages — `Sidera Funds "
"SICAV – Christian Equity*`, `European Corporate Green Bond*` — and print "
"the note at the foot of the page. The mark is part of the heading's text,"
" in the same font and the same size as the name, so no selection can "
"leave it out: it has to come off here, where the name is read, with a cut"
" **anchored at the end**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:184
msgid ""
"Anchored, because `A*B Fund` keeps its asterisk: that one is not a "
"footnote. A report that uses several marks lists them in the class, "
"`\\s*[*¹†]+\\s*$`; one that also writes `(continued)` on its continuation"
" pages joins the two, `\\(continued\\)|\\s*[*]+\\s*$`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:188
msgid ""
"It is not cosmetic. The name this pipe publishes *is* the sub-fund's "
"identity: it goes into `funds.csv`, into the `fund` field of every "
"holding on the page, and it is what every later phase — the statement of "
"net assets, the investment managers, the SFDR article — looks the sub-"
"fund up by. Those comparisons normalise the name, and normalisation does "
"**not** remove an asterisk, so `Christian Equity*` and `Christian Equity`"
" are two different sub-funds. A mark left on is therefore not a blemish "
"in one column: it is a row that quietly matches nothing and disappears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:195
msgid ""
"The same column exists for the statement of net assets, where the heading"
" carries the same mark for the same reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:198
msgid "Classification rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:200
msgid ""
"A classification row declares a page class and **one** header to look "
"for. Rows sharing an id describe one pipe, and the page belongs to that "
"class if it contains **all** of them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:209
msgid ""
"Two rows, one id, both required. Splitting a conjunction across rows "
"rather than packing it into one cell is what keeps these files editable "
"in a spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:212
msgid "Partial pipelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:214
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each of the three segments can be switched off **individually**. That is "
"what a *partial* pipeline is, and it is what makes the merge with the "
"other levels useful rather than theoretical: a format can take its "
"`pdf_extract` from here and its `text_filter` from a Python module, by "
"leaving the second unspecified at this level "
"({doc}`../../../reference/design/formats-as-plugins`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:219
msgid ""
"Every algorithm has the same table for it, `partial_pipes.csv` in its own"
" directory, with the same header:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:227
msgid ""
"`FALSE` switches a segment off; `TRUE` or an empty cell leaves it on, and"
" so does having no row at all. At most one row per pipe, and a row naming"
" a pipe the arguments do not declare is refused. The file is required "
"wherever the arguments are: a repository with `manco/args.csv` has "
"`manco/partial_pipes.csv` too, even if it holds only its header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:232
msgid ""
"A segment switched off may not be configured, and a cell a built segment "
"needs may not be empty. So each column belongs to the segment that reads "
"it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid ""
"the four selections, `Algorithm flags`, the two tolerances, the three "
"`Collapse` cells"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid ""
"the five column positions, `Geometrical indexing`, `Interpret dash as "
"zero`, `Remove from fund`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "the two `Interpret … as …` flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid ""
"the fund column and the three amounts (required), `Currency set`, `Date "
"set`, the three windows, `Drop set`, `Drop fund set`, `Table condition`, "
"`Algorithm flags`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`Date regex`, `Remove from fund`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`Amount cast`, `Date cast`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`Label set` (required), `Where`, `Take`, `Reach`, `Stop set`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`After`, `Before`, `Among`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`Also investments manager`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`Language` (required), `Product joined`, `Product prepend`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`Language` (required), the rows of `product_prefixes.csv`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "—"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md
msgid "`Class` (required), `Header set`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:243
msgid "Two consequences are worth stating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:245
msgid ""
"**A column read by two segments goes only with both.** The SFDR language "
"is read by the extraction and by the filter, so it stays required while "
"either is built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:248
msgid ""
"**A cell that refines another segment's cell is free when that segment is"
" off.** `Date regex` refines `Date set`, and `Among` chooses among the "
"lines `Take: all` hands over; with the extraction built elsewhere, the "
"cell they refine is empty by necessity, and what it would have said is "
"not this row's to say."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:253
msgid ""
"**A classification pipeline is a special case.** Its filter and its "
"deserializer take no parameter and there is one of each for the whole "
"pipeline, while each classifier has its own extraction. So `pdf_extract` "
"can be switched off per pipe, but the pipes of one pipeline must "
"**agree** on `text_filter` and `deserialize`: if they do not, loading "
"fails and names the two pipes. Building the segment as soon as any pipe "
"asked for it would be a rule written nowhere, covering a contradiction in"
" the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:260
msgid "Two conventions of the structured tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:261
msgid ""
"**An empty cell means *absent*, everywhere.** Not zero, not the default —"
" absent. It is the same rule the output files follow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/structured.md:264
msgid ""
"**Every validation error names the row number.** These files are edited "
"in a spreadsheet by people who are not reading Rust backtraces, and an "
"error that cannot say which row is nearly useless. It is also why the "
"repository's CSVs are parsed by hand rather than by a dataframe library."
msgstr ""

